# RTP audit — an ExactOdds casino rule pack.
#
# Return-to-player is the number regulators actually check: total paid out
# divided by total wagered, over the audit window. This program is the
# formula, published: the auditor takes the casino's own ledger totals,
# runs them through this program, and gets the exact RTP in basis points.
# 9600 means 96.00%. Same totals, same answer, on every seat.
#
# Rules: RTP = paid * 10000 / wagered, integer division floors. Reported in
# basis points so no decimal point — and no floats — ever appear.

def rtp_bps(wagered_cents: int, paid_cents: int) -> int do
    ret paid_cents * 10000 / wagered_cents
end

# Audited cases.
say(rtp_bps(1000000, 962500))
say(rtp_bps(500000, 485000))
say(rtp_bps(100000, 100000))
